(4557610, 654779, 44877, '<td valign="top">Let me echo Roz by saying I immediately knew this had to be yours. <br/> <br/>And as an aside... I''m curious to know from where you take these street shots - from a house? An office? The roof? Are you on a light pole? On top of a car? Wherever it is, there seem to be pedestrians that you can turn into wildly interesting images. Nobody walks the streets here - too far, too hot, too dangerous. <br/> <br/>The photo - as usual, underrated. As always, totally excellent. Beautifully seen and composed. Very funny with the Parking on the ground and the walkie sign right next to it. Great use of colors, too.</td>', 'Let me echo Roz by saying I immediately knew this had to be yours.  And as an aside... I''m curious to know from where you take these street shots - from a house? An office? The roof? Are you on a light pole? On top of a car? Wherever it is, there seem to be pedestrians that you can turn into wildly interesting images. Nobody walks the streets here - too far, too hot, too dangerous.  The photo - as usual, underrated. As always, totally excellent. Beautifully seen and composed. Very funny with the Parking on the ground and the walkie sign right next to it. Great use of colors, too.', '2008-03-12 09:51:40.000000', NULL, 0),
